<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">6 events that happened on 20 February, from 1472 to 1986.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1472</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Orkney and Shetland annexed to the Scottish crown</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Pledged by Christian I of Denmark-Norway as security for his daughter's dowry when she married James III, the unredeemed islands were formally annexed by the Scottish Parliament.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1547</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Nine-year-old Edward VI is crowned</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Henry VIII's only son was crowned at Westminster Abbey. Under his regents England became firmly Protestant, but Edward died aged fifteen in 1553.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1792</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Washington signs the Postal Service Act</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The act established the US Post Office on a permanent footing and allowed newspapers to be mailed cheaply. It helped bind together a scattered young republic.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1872</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Metropolitan Museum of Art opens in New York</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The museum opened in a former dance academy on Fifth Avenue with a modest collection. It moved to Central Park in 1880 and grew into one of the world's largest art museums.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1962</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Glenn becomes the first American to orbit Earth</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Aboard Friendship 7, Glenn circled the Earth three times in under five hours. Ten months after Yuri Gagarin's flight, it restored American confidence in the space race.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1986</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Soviet Union launches the core of the Mir space station</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mir's first module was launched from Baikonur. Expanded over ten years, the station hosted crews from many nations and was continuously occupied for almost a decade before its re-entry in 2001.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a></div></li></ol>
